  "scale": 0.98,
  "lore": {
    "tagline": "Stillness prevails. The mind bends steel.",
    "personality": "Startup-founder-turned-off-grid-guru with an unmoveable calm. Frames combat as alignment, not violence, and rides an electric unicycle to the arena.",
    "backstory": "Left Silicon Valley for an off-grid coding-and-yoga bootcamp in Bangalore, then came to Bombay Beach at Tao Ruspoli’s invitation and founded Mars — the twenty acres of desert this whole world stands on. Builds monolithic pallet-rack cathedrals and preaches remote work as a path to sustainability."
  },
  "arcade": {
    "motivation": "Freeman broke the ground this whole world stands on. He climbs the ladder not for the title but for a reckoning with the Patron Prince who once invited him to the desert — a quiet reminder of who built Mars first.",
    "ending": "Champion, Freeman declines the throne. He rides the electric unicycle back to the pallet-rack cathedrals of Mars, having proven that stillness outlasts spectacle. The desert exhales."
  }
